hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27631","Haddathana Yazid ibn Harun, he said: Haddathana Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, that Salih Abu al-Khalil narrated to him from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal, that Umm Hakim bint al-Zubayr narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon Duba'ah bint al-Zubayr and ate of a shoulder with her, then he prayed and did not perform ablution from that."
"27632","Haddathana Hasan ibn Musa, he said: Haddathana Rafi' ibn Salamah al-Ashja'i, he said: Hashraj ibn Ziyad narrated to me from his grandmother, mother of his father, she said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the campaign of Khaybar, and I was the sixth of six women. She said: So it reached the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that women were with him. She said: So he sent to us and called us. She said: So we saw anger in his face, and he said: What brought you out, and by whose command did you come out? We said: We came out with you to hand the arrows and to give sawiq to drink, and with us is medicine for wounds, and we spin hair so we may help therewith in the path of Allah. He said: Stand and go back. She said: Then when Allah conquered Khaybar for him, he brought out for us from it shares like the shares of men. So I said to her: O my grandmother, what did he bring out for you? She said: Dates."
